===Adjective===
{{en-adj|concreter}}

# [[real#Adjective|Real]], [[actual#Adjective|actual]], [[tangible#Adjective|tangible]].
#: {{ux|en|Fuzzy videotapes and distorted sound recordings are not '''concrete''' evidence that Bigfoot exists.}}
#: {{ux|en|Once arrested, I realized that handcuffs are '''concrete''', even if my concept of what is legal wasn’t.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Denis Campbell|title=Hospital staff 'lack skills to cope with dementia patients'|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230405175631/https://www.theguardian.com/society/2011/dec/16/hospital-staff-dementia-patients|date=16 December 2011|passage=Professor Peter Crome, chair of the audit's steering group, said the report "provides further '''concrete''' evidence that the care of patients with dementia in hospital is in need of a radical shake-up". While a few hospitals had risen to the challenge of improving patients' experiences, many have not, he said. The report recommends that all staff receive basic dementia awareness training, and staffing levels should be maintained to help such patients.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=James Zogby|authorlink=James Zogby|title=Israel's prickliness blocks the long quest for peace|work=[[w:The National (Abu Dhabi)|The National]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220120211355/https://www.thenationalnews.com/opinion/israel-s-prickliness-blocks-the-long-quest-for-peace-1.197448/he-long-quest-for-peace-1.197448/|date=6 February 2016|passage=The secretary general went on to express his concern with recent Israeli announcements to expand settlements in the occupied lands, urging them to: stop the demolitions of Palestinian homes and confiscation of Palestinian lands, address the humanitarian situation in Gaza and to take '''concrete''' steps to improve the daily lives of the Palestinian people. He also noted that all of these behaviours made more difficult the achievement of an Israel-Palestinian peace.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|author=Julian E. Barnes|title=White House Official Says Huawei Has Secret Back Door to Extract Data|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230604134348/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/02/11/us/politics/white-house-huawei-back-door.html|date=11 February 2020|passage=American intelligence officials have long said privately that Huawei has so-called back doors that could allow the company to obtain data that flows on the networks they build and maintain. But publicly, officials have spoken mostly about the potential that Huawei could provide Chinese officials with access to all kinds of data, without offering '''concrete''' proof.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Blake Brittain|title=AI-generated art cannot be copyrighted under U.S. law, court rules|work={{w|The Globe and Mail}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230823053953/https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/international-business/us-business/article-ai-generated-art-cannot-receive-copyrights-under-us-law-court-rules/|location=Toronto, ON|publisher={{w|The Woodbridge Company}}|date=21 August 2023|issn=0319-0714|oclc=6155622|passage=Mr. Thaler challenged the decision in federal court, arguing that human authorship is not a '''concrete''' legal requirement and allowing AI copyrights would be in line with copyright's purpose as outlined in the U.S. constitution to "promote the progress of science and useful arts."}}
# Being or applying to actual things, rather than [[abstract]] qualities or categories.
#: {{ant|en|intangible|abstract}}
#* {{RQ:Watts Logick|passage='''''Concrete''''' Terms, while they expreſs the Quality, do alſo either expreſs, or imply, or refer to ſome Subject to which it belongs; as ''white'', ''round'', ''long'', ''broad'', ''wiſe'', ''mortal'', ''living'', ''dead''.|page=58}}
#* {{RQ:Mill System of Logic|chapter=Fallacies of Confusion|volume=II|page=465|passage=As expressed in the premiss, the proposition appeals directly and in '''concrete''' language to the incapacity of the human imagination for conceiving a minimum. }}
#* {{RQ:New Yorker|author=James Wood|authorlink=James Wood (critic)|quotee=Gianna Pomata|title=Sergei Dovlatov and the Hearsay of Memory|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230811082328/https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2020/07/20/how-pandemics-wreak-havoc-and-open-minds|date=7 April 2014|passage=Bologna was a stronghold of medical teaching. The city's famous university, established in 1088, is the oldest in the world. "What they had we call scholastic medicine," Pomata told me. "When we say 'scholastic,' we mean something that is very abstract, not '''concrete''', not empirical."}}
# [[particular#Adjective|Particular]], [[specific#Adjective|specific]], rather than [[general#Adjective|general]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:specific}}
#: {{ant|en|Thesaurus:generic}}
#: {{ux|en|While everyone else offered thoughts and prayers, she made a '''concrete''' proposal to help.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''concrete''' ideas}}
#* {{RQ:Rolling Stone|author=Emily Zemler|quotee={{w|Soccer Mommy}}|title=Soccer Mommy Searches for Freedom With 'Feel It All the Time' on 'Kimmel'|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221006235133/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/soccer-mommy-feel-it-all-the-time-kimmel-1234580678/|date=24 August 2022|passage=Nothing is really permanent. But, at the same time, so many things are forever. For me, that's always been something that's hard to grasp, because I'm a very '''concrete''' thinker. I want to be like, 'This is how things are, and there's a reason.'}}
#* {{RQ:Independent|author=Abe Asher|title=Trudeau suggests link between four shot-down objects despite US playing down connection|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230320054426/https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/justin-trudeau-four-objects-shot-down-b2281562.html|date=13 February 2023|passage=In his remarks to reporters, Mr Trudeau offered few '''concrete''' details but was more willing to make a connection between the downed objects. He said he would discuss the issue further with Mr Biden at a scheduled meeting in March.}}
# United by [[coalescence#Noun|coalescence]] of separate particles, or liquid, into one [[mass#Noun|mass]] or [[solid#Noun|solid]].
#: {{ant|en|discrete}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Thomas Burnet|authorlink=Thomas Burnet|chapter=IV|title=The Theory Of The Earth:{{nb...|Containing an Account of the Original of the Earth, and of All the General Changes which it Hath Already Undergone, Or is to Undergo, Till the Consummation of All Things.}}|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed by}} R. Norton, for Walter Kettilby,{{nb...|At the Biſhops-Head in S. Paul's Church-Yard}}|year=1684|volume_plain=Book I|page=51|pageurl=https://books.google.ca/books?id=a78yYe0NZuEC&pg=PA51|passage=So that the firſt '''concrete''' ſtate or conſiſtent ſurface of the Chaos, muſt be of the ſame form or figure with the laſt liquid ſtate it was in; for that is the mould, as it were, upon which it is caſt; as the ſhell of an Egg is of the like form with the ſurface of the liquor it lies upon.}}
# {{lb|en|not comparable}} Made of concrete (building material).
#: {{ux|en|The office building had '''concrete''' flower boxes out front.}}
#* {{RQ:Smith Swing Time|page=46|passage=I took the stairs down to the communal area and stood resting against a concrete pillar, watching my “brother” kick up little scraps of half-frozen turf.}}
#* {{RQ:Telegraph|author=Martin Chilton|title=The tragedy of Ivan, the 'shopping mall gorilla' who drove America wild|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20211209024700/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/films/0/tragedy-ivan-shopping-mall-gorilla-drove-america-wild/|date=21 August 2020|passage=The video images of him banging on the '''concrete''' walls of his cell are wretched. The story of Ivan's plight was covered by everyone from People Magazine to the New York Times, who reported on the "sulking gorilla with matted hair" trapped in his '''concrete''' prison.}}

